The following are multiple choice questions (with answers) about formal logic.

 Select the best translation into predicate logic.Some robbers steal money from a bank. (Bx: x is a bank; Mx: x is money; Rx: x is a robber; Sxyz: x steals y from z)
A. (∃x){Bx • (∃y)[Ry • (∀z)(Mz ⊃ Syzx)]}
B. (∃x)(∃y)(∃z)[(Rx • By) • (Mz • Syxz)]
C. (∃x){Rx ⊃ (∃y)[My ⊃ (∃z)(Bz ⊃ Sxyz)]}
D. (∃x){Rx • (∃y)[My • (∃z)(Bz • Sxyz)]}
Answer:
